# Four rigid-water-like molecules for the constrained NVT validation case.
#
# Units follow the GMD molecular .ff convention (see src/io/config_loader.cpp):
# energies in kcal/mol, distances in Angstrom, angles in degrees.
#
# THE BONDED FORCE CONSTANTS ARE DELIBERATELY ZERO. The bonds and angles in
# cluster.top exist only to exclude the intramolecular non-bonded pairs (1-2 via
# the O-H bonds, 1-3 via the H-O-H angle). The molecular geometry is held
# entirely by the distance constraints.
#
# The INTERMOLECULAR Lennard-Jones terms are real and are what make this case
# different from constrained_nve_water: the force providers report a non-zero
# virial, so the constraint virial is added to a genuine partner rather than to
# a tensor of zeros.
#
# Charges are zero, so there is no Coulomb term and no PME grid is involved --
# the case runs with no external engine and no long-range solver.
force_field molecular

lj_cutoff 8.0

type 1 O mass 15.9994 epsilon 0.1521 sigma 3.1507 charge 0.0
type 2 H mass 1.0080  epsilon 0.0460 sigma 0.4000 charge 0.0

# Exclusion-only terms; see above.
bond_type 1 k 0.0 r0 0.9572
angle_type 1 k 0.0 theta0 104.52
